# A dependency whose package holds no file for any operating system but Windows,
# imported by a module that puts no build constraint on the import.
#
# Which files a package is built from is decided by build constraints, and GOOS
# is one of them. Under GOOS=linux the import below resolves to a
# golang.org/x/sys/windows with nothing in it, and the load fails:
#
#	-: build constraints exclude all Go files in .../golang.org/x/sys@v0.20.0/windows
#
# That takes the whole module with it. A repository whose target is Windows
# cannot be read at all by a run that only ever looks at it as Linux, and the
# run exits 1 on a module whose owner has nothing to fix.
#
# Every error the load raised is an exclusion, which is what an operating system
# the module does not target looks like, so those scans are passed over rather
# than failing the module. The Windows scan reads the module and finds
# GO-2026-5024, which is what the diff and the report assert. A run that scanned
# under one operating system would exit 1 here and change nothing.
-- go.mod --
module example.com/root

go 1.25.0

require golang.org/x/sys v0.20.0
-- go.sum --
golang.org/x/sys v0.20.0 h1:Od9JTbYCk261bKm4M/mw7AklTlFYIa0bIp9BgSm1S8Y=
golang.org/x/sys v0.20.0/go.mod h1:/VUhepiaJMQUp4+oa/7Zr1D23ma6VTLIYjOOTFZPUcA=
-- main.go --
package main

// The import carries no build constraint of its own, so the package it names
// has to resolve under every operating system the module is scanned under, and
// golang.org/x/sys/windows resolves under only one of them.
import "golang.org/x/sys/windows"

func main() { println(windows.NewLazySystemDLL("kernel32.dll").Name) }
-- want_diff.txt --
diff --git a/go.mod b/go.mod
index 11abaad..88abbe9 100644
--- a/go.mod
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -2,4 +2,4 @@ module example.com/root
 
 go 1.25.0
 
-require golang.org/x/sys v0.20.0
+require golang.org/x/sys v0.44.0
diff --git a/go.sum b/go.sum
index 5d1e088..0e11bfe 100644
--- a/go.sum
+++ b/go.sum
@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
-golang.org/x/sys v0.20.0 h1:Od9JTbYCk261bKm4M/mw7AklTlFYIa0bIp9BgSm1S8Y=
-golang.org/x/sys v0.20.0/go.mod h1:/VUhepiaJMQUp4+oa/7Zr1D23ma6VTLIYjOOTFZPUcA=
+golang.org/x/sys v0.44.0 h1:ildZl3J4uzeKP07r2F++Op7E9B29JRUy+a27EibtBTQ=
+golang.org/x/sys v0.44.0/go.mod h1:4GL1E5IUh+htKOUEOaiffhrAeqysfVGipDYzABqnCmw=
-- want_report.md --
govulncheck found 1 vulnerability; this PR fixes 1:

**[GO-2026-5024](https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5024)**: Integer overflow in NewNTUnicodeString in golang.org/x/sys/windows

    golang.org/x/sys v0.20.0 -> v0.44.0
